1
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:10,960
20 YEARS AGO

2
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:13,360
<i>Mr. Kiat, you took my child and ran away!</i>

3
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:29,800
<i>Dad, I told you, you didn't</i>
<i>have to buy me anything this year.</i>

4
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:32,320
<i>You can't stop me, sweetheart.</i>

5
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:37,360
<i>Oh my! Is this another</i>
<i>ten-million-baht check in a box?</i>

6
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:38,560
<i>Whoa!</i>

7
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:41,960
<i>Open it. Go on. Open it, Alyssa.</i>

8
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:49,600
<i>Oh my! You really went all out this year.</i>

9
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:51,480
<i>You even got her a land title deed.</i>

10
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:53,760
<i>Where is the land?</i>

11
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:55,840
<i>Look, everyone! See?</i>

12
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:59,440
<i>She got a land title deed! Look at this!</i>

13
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:01,400
<i>Alyssa!</i>

14
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:10,760
Let's go.

15
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:17,440
Take lots of pictures, Wee.
I'm already excited for you.

16
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:20,640
I know. Hope you find
the book you're looking for.

17
00:04:21,279 --> 00:04:23,160
-Good luck.
-You should go now.

18
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,280
Bye.

19
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:27,880
UNIVERSITY LIBRARY

20
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:23,720
Sorry.

21
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:36,120
What should we do? There's only one copy.

22
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:41,760
It's okay. You take it first.

23
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:44,840
I'm going to borrow it and take it home.

24
00:05:49,960 --> 00:05:52,880
How about this? I'll make a copy of it,

25
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:55,520
then give this one to you. How about that?

26
00:05:57,160 --> 00:06:00,040
No, it's okay. I'll make the copy myself.

27
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,400
Are you sure?

28
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:06,760
Yes. I'm from out of town.

29
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:08,880
It'd be hard to return it later.

30
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:11,560
I'll make the copy myself.

31
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:17,040
Thank you.

32
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:19,080
Yes.

33
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:37,560
SELF-SERVICE PRINTING
COPYING AND SCANNING

34
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:38,720
Here you go.

35
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:40,560
Thank you.

36
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:51,280
It's okay.

37
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:18,120
Want to use this to hold them together?

38
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:19,800
Oh.

39
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:28,160
Thank you so much.

40
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:31,840
Thank you for taking the time
to make the copies.

41
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,040
No problem. Anyway, enjoy reading it.

42
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:39,680
This academic book?

43
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:44,280
Yes.

44
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:13,600
Yes, Uncle Jak.

45
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:16,840
I'm at the library.

46
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:21,880
It's okay. I'll go myself.

47
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:23,720
Yes.

48
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:41,039
My mom says you'll get sick
if your head gets wet.

49
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:46,560
It's okay, really.

50
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:51,880
Don't worry about it.
Consider it a trade for this one.

51
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:57,240
Thank you.

52
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:02,520
If we meet again,

53
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:05,320
maybe we can trade them back.

54
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:10,440
I hope we get that chance.

55
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:04,000
Sign here.

56
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:06,600
RAWEE WITTAYADUMRONG - PLAYER

57
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:27,400
Hello, Uncle Jak.

58
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:30,800
Have a seat, Alyssa.

59
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:36,360
How was the traffic?

60
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:40,040
A little. It started raining.

61
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:43,520
What did you want to talk to me about?

62
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:47,240
Let's order something to eat first.

63
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:50,160
Consider it my belated birthday treat.

64
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:52,520
The menu, please.

65
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:55,680
Thank you.

66
00:10:58,520 --> 00:10:59,880
Alyssa.

67
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:02,040
A birthday gift from me.

68
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:04,320
Thank you.

69
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:07,160
Go ahead, open it. See if you like it.

70
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:09,320
I put a lot of thought into choosing it.

71
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:27,160
This pen is from a great brand.

72
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:32,880
It writes smoothly.
You can use it for writing or…

73
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:36,960
even signing for your inheritance
from your father.

74
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:43,480
Not funny? I'm just joking.

75
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:47,880
Uncle Jak, just tell me
what you wanted to say.

76
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:50,200
Otherwise, we'll just waste more time.

77
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:55,560
I heard

78
00:11:56,400 --> 00:11:59,680
your father gave you land
as a birthday gift.

79
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:02,800
Who told you?

80
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:07,560
It doesn't matter who told me.
Is it true or not?

81
00:12:07,640 --> 00:12:12,360
Have you seen where it is yet?
What will you do with it?

82
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:16,120
Near the main market.
I haven't gone to see it yet.

83
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:18,480
And has the transfer been completed?

84
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:22,760
Is there something you want?

85
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:26,480
Have you decided
what you're going to do with that land?

86
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:32,240
You haven't figured it out yet?

87
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:34,680
That's not surprising. You're still young.

88
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:39,000
I don't think I need to rush.

89
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:40,640
The land isn't going anywhere.

90
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,640
But if you leave it unused,
I think it'll lose value.

91
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:47,720
How about this?

92
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:51,840
Leave it with me for now. I promise

93
00:12:51,920 --> 00:12:54,520
I'll make a good profit from it.

94
00:12:55,640 --> 00:12:59,560
I think you should talk to my father
about it yourself.

95
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:03,240
Alyssa.

96
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:09,280
You know how your father
has always kept his assets from me.

97
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:13,120
Well, I'll be honest.

98
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:16,640
I've had my eye on this land
since last year.

99
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:19,600
I already have a business plan for it.

100
00:13:19,680 --> 00:13:24,160
Honestly, this land
should have been mine in the first place.

101
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:29,640
But I understand. Of course, a father
would give his assets to his child.

102
00:13:29,720 --> 00:13:31,880
I'm just disappointed.

103
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:34,440
It feels like
I don't even exist in this family.

104
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:38,000
What do you want me to do?

105
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:41,760
Give the land to me.

106
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:42,840
Well…

107
00:13:44,040 --> 00:13:45,920
I don't want any other piece of land.

108
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,440
This one means a lot to me.

109
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:53,840
Besides, you're still young.
You don't know what to do with it, do you?

110
00:13:53,920 --> 00:13:57,840
Wouldn't it be better
to let me put it to good use?

111
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:01,600
I'll talk to my father about it.

112
00:14:01,680 --> 00:14:04,200
Whoa. Don't.

113
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:05,960
Don't do that, Alyssa.

114
00:14:06,040 --> 00:14:07,960
If you go and talk to that old man,

115
00:14:08,040 --> 00:14:11,840
he'll just accuse me
of trying to take your property again.

116
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:16,440
-So you'll transfer it to--
-I'll take care of it.

117
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:18,800
Thank you for the gift,

118
00:14:18,880 --> 00:14:21,840
but I'll have to pass on this meal.

119
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:25,760
I'm still full. I'll be going now.

120
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:29,760
Goodbye.

121
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:52,360
Alright.

122
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:02,840
-Thank you, Uncle.
-You're welcome.

123
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,480
-Here's the key.
-Thank you so much, Uncle.

124
00:15:07,560 --> 00:15:08,520
-Goodbye.
-Okay.

125
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:10,680
-See you again.
-See you.

126
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:16,920
Mom, the club's football player is here!

127
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:21,840
-Everything went well, right, Wee?
-Yes, Mom.

128
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:25,200
-Good job, son.
-Thank you.

129
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:27,840
Sorry your dad and I couldn't go
with you today.

130
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:32,160
It's okay, Mom.
You can still come to my first match.

131
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:34,880
I also got a scholarship, Mom.

132
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:39,360
-Great job, son. My son is the best.
-Thank you.

133
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:44,800
Good job. You're amazing.

134
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:49,240
Ow, Mom.

135
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:52,000
My leg hurts. It really hurts.

136
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:55,440
-Where does it hurt? Is it serious?
-Well…

137
00:15:56,160 --> 00:16:00,160
Here and here, Mom.

138
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:01,760
You little rascal.

139
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:04,840
-I just want some attention.
-Stealing the show again, brat?

140
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:07,560
Come here. Go take a shower.

141
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:09,360
-What are you doing, Wee?
-We're decorating the house.

142
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:12,040
-Easy. My leg hurts, Wee.
-Hurry up and take a shower.

143
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:14,080
-I want to hug Mom.
-You might really get hurt.

144
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:16,040
-Can I hug Mom first?
-Come on. Go take a shower.

145
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:18,920
-Ow! It hurts.
-We're setting up for your birthday.

146
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,440
-Come on. Mom, look.
-What? No.

147
00:16:21,520 --> 00:16:23,320
-Korn is being stubborn again.
-Wait!

148
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:26,960
-Go shower, Korn. Hurry, little brother.
-Ugh! Wee!

149
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:28,440
-Careful, son.
-No. Come back and cuddle Mom later.

150
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:30,240
-Go shower. Mom can smell you already.
-Mom.

151
00:16:30,320 --> 00:16:31,880
Mom, look.

152
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:34,640
Whoa, Wee. I just wanted
to get some love from Mom.

153
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:47,960
Kiat, leaving already?

154
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:50,880
Yes. It's my son's birthday today.

155
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:52,000
Korn.

156
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:54,760
Korn? Is he the older one
or the younger one?

157
00:16:54,840 --> 00:16:56,280
The younger one.

158
00:16:56,360 --> 00:17:00,200
And the older one
is your younger sister's child, right?

159
00:17:00,280 --> 00:17:02,440
-Oh, yes.
-What's his name?

160
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:04,119
-Rawee.
-Rawee.

161
00:17:05,079 --> 00:17:06,240
Wait a moment.

162
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:10,680
Here. This is for Korn's birthday.

163
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:13,079
You don't have to. It's okay.

164
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:15,319
Take it. I want to give it to your son.

165
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:16,920
-Thank you.
-Sure.

166
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:19,720
Then I'll get going.

167
00:17:19,800 --> 00:17:21,800
-Go ahead.
-I ordered a cake from the cake shop.

168
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:23,200
-I need to pick it up before they close.
-Sure.

169
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:25,040
-Alright. Go ahead.
-Thank you.

170
00:17:25,119 --> 00:17:26,280
-Take care.
-Yes.

171
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:56,400
Let me see that.

172
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:58,840
-Wee, that's mine. Don't touch it.
-Wait. Let me see it, Korn.

173
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:01,400
Wait, Korn. Let me see it first.

174
00:18:01,480 --> 00:18:04,200
-No. Don't touch it.
-Wait, Korn.

175
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:06,800
Who gave this to you?

176
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:08,480
It's got a little flower on it.

177
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:11,120
Huh?

178
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:15,280
-Wait. Answer me first. Okay.
-No one.

179
00:18:19,280 --> 00:18:21,720
It's my friend's. She gave it to me.

180
00:18:22,360 --> 00:18:25,200
Here. It's for holding
the photocopies together.

181
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:29,840
Wait, where's my hat?

182
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:36,240
Well,

183
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:37,560
I lent it to my friend.

184
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:43,160
It was raining,
so I just let her borrow it.

185
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:46,480
Is she the same person
who gave you this hair tie?

186
00:18:50,040 --> 00:18:53,720
Now I really want to see her.
What girl gave this to you?

187
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:56,200
Huh, my little brother?

188
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:59,520
-Enough. Go, Wee.
-Hey.

189
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:01,080
-Go change your clothes.
-What's with you?

190
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:04,160
-Get out! I'll tell Mom.
-You're acting suspicious, Korn. Wait!

191
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:05,640
-Korn! Mom!
-Go!

192
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:07,000
Mom!

193
00:19:08,120 --> 00:19:09,800
-Korn, open the door for me.
-No.

194
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:10,920
-Mom!
-That's enough.

195
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:14,680
-Mom, Korn has a girl!
-Go get dressed. We're going to be late.

196
00:19:14,760 --> 00:19:17,360
Sure it was just the rain?

197
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:19,720
Yeah, that's it. Now go get dressed.

198
00:19:19,800 --> 00:19:21,160
Fine.

199
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:24,280
-I'm going to shower now.
-Alright. Hurry up.

200
00:19:24,360 --> 00:19:26,800
-Really?
-Yeah, hurry.

201
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,600
We're gonna be late.

202
00:19:33,760 --> 00:19:36,600
-Mom! Korn has a girl!
-Wee!

203
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:37,600
Enough.

204
00:19:46,320 --> 00:19:51,040
HAPPY BIRTHDAY PHAKORN

205
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:53,320
Thank you.

206
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:54,800
Some candles too, please.

207
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:57,800
Thank you.

208
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:53,240
HAPPY BIRTHDAY PHAKORN

209
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:57,520
Korn, are you done yet? Come downstairs.

210
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:02,480
I'm done.

211
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:10,960
Korn, are you ready yet?

212
00:21:11,040 --> 00:21:13,560
-Why are you in such a hurry?
-Hurry up.

213
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:17,360
Wait, come here. Close your eyes first.

214
00:21:18,240 --> 00:21:20,080
-Walk slowly.
-Is that really necessary?

215
00:21:20,160 --> 00:21:22,080
Just trust me. Hurry.

216
00:21:22,160 --> 00:21:24,600
-I can't see anything.
-Walk slowly.

217
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:28,960
-Are we there yet?
-Almost.

218
00:21:31,320 --> 00:21:32,720
Just a little further.

219
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:35,960
-Keep your eyes closed. Wait a second.
-Okay.

220
00:21:36,880 --> 00:21:39,280
One, two, three.

221
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:44,880
How is it?

222
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:49,000
I put this together with my snack money.
This is all I could do.

223
00:21:54,840 --> 00:21:57,600
-Whoa.
-It's okay.

224
00:21:58,200 --> 00:22:00,040
Just celebrating together like this,

225
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:01,640
I'm already happy.

226
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:06,560
-You're such a jerk.
-A sweet jerk.

227
00:22:08,280 --> 00:22:09,480
Thank you, Wee.

228
00:22:09,560 --> 00:22:13,040
Guys, the food is ready.
Come help bring it out.

229
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:14,640
Yes, Mom.

230
00:22:17,560 --> 00:22:18,680
Thank you.

231
00:22:21,040 --> 00:22:23,360
Did your dad go help them with the cake?

232
00:22:23,440 --> 00:22:24,680
He's still not back.

233
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:29,800
Here you go.

234
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:33,040
Delicious.

235
00:22:37,360 --> 00:22:40,560
When will Dad be back, Mom?
It's been a while.

236
00:22:41,960 --> 00:22:43,560
Give your dad a call.

237
00:22:44,360 --> 00:22:45,360
-Okay.
-Yeah.

238
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:48,120
Dad's here, Mom.

239
00:22:55,800 --> 00:22:57,160
Mom!

240
00:23:16,880 --> 00:23:19,440
PATIENT REGISTRATION

241
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:23,920
How is my dad?

242
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:25,720
My dad's name is Kiat Wittayadamrong.

243
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:28,960
My husband is safe, right?

244
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:31,960
The stab wound was very deep.

245
00:23:32,040 --> 00:23:34,480
Mr. Kiat was brought
to the hospital too late.

246
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:37,360
We did everything we could to save him.

247
00:23:38,320 --> 00:23:39,640
I'm sorry for your loss.

248
00:24:09,040 --> 00:24:11,880
Wake up, Dad.

249
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:20,160
Dad.

250
00:24:20,240 --> 00:24:22,680
It's my birthday today.

251
00:24:36,080 --> 00:24:37,840
Worst birthday ever!

252
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:39,840
Korn, don't! Stop!

253
00:24:39,920 --> 00:24:41,840
-Listen to me first!
-Leave me alone!

254
00:25:03,040 --> 00:25:06,600
Wee! Let him go for now.

255
00:25:06,680 --> 00:25:08,080
Give him some space.

256
00:25:39,480 --> 00:25:44,480
PHAKORN

257
00:26:02,040 --> 00:26:03,720
No!

258
00:26:13,520 --> 00:26:16,200
Go to sleep, son. Dad's right here.

259
00:26:36,560 --> 00:26:41,480
Korn said someone teased you today
about being adopted?

260
00:26:42,080 --> 00:26:43,160
Yes, Dad.

261
00:26:44,800 --> 00:26:46,360
Were you angry at your friend?

262
00:26:46,440 --> 00:26:49,200
No, Dad. Why would I be angry?

263
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:51,120
It's the truth.

264
00:26:52,200 --> 00:26:53,680
I'm proud of you, son.

265
00:26:55,240 --> 00:26:57,360
Even though you're adopted,

266
00:26:57,440 --> 00:27:01,080
-Mom and I love you like our own.
-Yes.

267
00:27:02,240 --> 00:27:04,920
The four of us are a family, okay?

268
00:27:05,520 --> 00:27:06,760
Yes.

269
00:27:11,040 --> 00:27:13,280
You have to love your little brother

270
00:27:13,360 --> 00:27:15,640
and help Mom and Dad
take care of him, okay?

271
00:27:15,720 --> 00:27:16,600
Yes.

272
00:27:16,680 --> 00:27:20,280
Knowing how strong you are,
I don't have to worry anymore.

273
00:27:20,920 --> 00:27:23,640
-Yes.
-Good job, son.

274
00:27:57,560 --> 00:27:58,840
Wee.

275
00:28:03,840 --> 00:28:05,120
This morning…

276
00:28:07,840 --> 00:28:10,920
I should've hugged Dad
before he left for work.

277
00:28:12,680 --> 00:28:13,960
Go to sleep, Korn.

278
00:28:15,720 --> 00:28:17,800
We still have a lot to do tomorrow.

279
00:28:19,880 --> 00:28:21,560
I can't sleep.

280
00:28:55,760 --> 00:28:58,720
Go to sleep, Korn. Dad…

281
00:29:00,440 --> 00:29:01,920
I'm right here.

282
00:29:42,440 --> 00:29:45,200
From now on,
help take care of Kiat's family.

283
00:29:45,800 --> 00:29:48,360
-If they need anything, let me know.
-Yes, sir.

284
00:29:48,440 --> 00:29:51,400
I heard his wife doesn't work,
and he has two children, right?

285
00:29:51,480 --> 00:29:53,200
-Yes, sir.
-Alright.

286
00:29:53,280 --> 00:29:54,720
-I'm counting on you.
-Yes, sir.

287
00:30:00,800 --> 00:30:01,840
Dad.

288
00:30:02,680 --> 00:30:05,760
Oh, Alyssa. I thought
you weren't coming home this week.

289
00:30:06,680 --> 00:30:10,080
I need to talk to you
about something important, Dad.

290
00:30:10,160 --> 00:30:13,160
But who was the funeral for?

291
00:30:13,760 --> 00:30:16,680
The factory's chief accountant.
You wouldn't know him.

292
00:30:19,520 --> 00:30:21,720
What did you want to talk to me about?

293
00:30:25,080 --> 00:30:27,760
I don't want the land
at the market anymore.

294
00:30:28,680 --> 00:30:31,000
Why, sweetheart? What happened?

295
00:30:32,200 --> 00:30:33,720
I don't think

296
00:30:33,800 --> 00:30:35,960
it would be useful to me right now.

297
00:30:36,040 --> 00:30:39,480
I think you should give it to someone
who can make use of it instead.

298
00:30:40,480 --> 00:30:41,560
Alyssa.

299
00:30:42,480 --> 00:30:46,440
You know you can always come to me

300
00:30:46,520 --> 00:30:48,400
if you have any problems.

301
00:30:49,080 --> 00:30:52,560
I don't want to fight
with my family over property.

302
00:30:52,640 --> 00:30:54,320
You're not taking anything from anyone.

303
00:30:54,400 --> 00:30:56,520
It's something you were meant to have.

304
00:30:58,280 --> 00:31:00,080
Uncle Jak wants this land.

305
00:31:01,680 --> 00:31:02,720
Alyssa.

306
00:31:04,160 --> 00:31:07,600
I gave this land to you
because you're my daughter.

307
00:31:08,200 --> 00:31:10,880
Everything I've done
has only been for you.

308
00:31:10,960 --> 00:31:12,760
Everyone else is just someone else.

309
00:31:15,160 --> 00:31:17,440
I don't want you to fight with Uncle Jak.

310
00:31:18,680 --> 00:31:20,400
We have so much land already.

311
00:31:20,480 --> 00:31:22,680
Just give it to him.
Let's end this problem.

312
00:31:22,760 --> 00:31:25,160
This problem won't end there, sweetheart.

313
00:31:26,560 --> 00:31:30,600
I don't want you getting involved
in family issues.

314
00:31:31,240 --> 00:31:33,360
Just focus on your studies
and enjoy yourself.

315
00:31:34,320 --> 00:31:36,200
I'll handle everything else.

316
00:31:37,440 --> 00:31:39,520
I didn't want to know about this either,

317
00:31:40,320 --> 00:31:43,400
but now that I'm involved,

318
00:31:43,480 --> 00:31:45,440
I want to be clear.

319
00:31:45,520 --> 00:31:47,520
I don't want to fight
with anyone over property.

320
00:31:49,000 --> 00:31:50,720
I don't want it.

321
00:31:51,760 --> 00:31:54,000
I really don't, Dad. I don't want it.

322
00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:57,080
Please keep it.

323
00:32:07,800 --> 00:32:09,360
This isn't what I wanted.

324
00:32:10,200 --> 00:32:13,840
I wanted the land at the market.
I never wanted to sell my company shares.

325
00:32:15,040 --> 00:32:17,800
Why do you think
I'd give you everything you want?

326
00:32:17,880 --> 00:32:20,520
You want the land at the market.

327
00:32:20,600 --> 00:32:22,520
Then you'll have to pay for it yourself.

328
00:32:23,760 --> 00:32:24,840
Here.

329
00:32:24,920 --> 00:32:26,760
Sign over your shares to me

330
00:32:27,720 --> 00:32:29,680
and take the land you want.

331
00:32:31,800 --> 00:32:33,160
You're pressuring me.

332
00:32:34,040 --> 00:32:35,160
Have you ever seen me
as your younger brother?

333
00:32:35,240 --> 00:32:37,720
Have you ever seen me
as your older brother?

334
00:32:38,960 --> 00:32:41,520
Have you ever thought
of Alyssa as your niece?

335
00:32:42,160 --> 00:32:44,080
You pressured a young girl over land

336
00:32:44,160 --> 00:32:46,040
that wasn't even yours to begin with.

337
00:32:46,960 --> 00:32:48,960
What the hell were you thinking, Jak?

338
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:53,120
You've already wasted
your share of the inheritance.

339
00:32:53,200 --> 00:32:56,480
I still gave you a place in the company,

340
00:32:56,560 --> 00:32:57,760
even a position at the factory.

341
00:32:58,560 --> 00:32:59,960
That should be more than enough.

342
00:33:00,600 --> 00:33:03,680
-What more do you want?
-I'm not selling my shares.

343
00:33:03,760 --> 00:33:05,440
These are the shares you gave me.

344
00:33:05,520 --> 00:33:06,760
I'm not selling them.

345
00:33:06,840 --> 00:33:09,280
And I should still own half the company.

346
00:33:09,360 --> 00:33:10,360
I'm not asking you.

347
00:33:11,560 --> 00:33:13,200
I'm telling you.

348
00:33:16,920 --> 00:33:19,960
Sign it. Sign!

349
00:33:20,040 --> 00:33:21,240
If you don't,

350
00:33:21,320 --> 00:33:25,480
I'll take everything back.
I won't even need to involve the law.

351
00:33:26,120 --> 00:33:27,520
You know I can do it.

352
00:33:30,040 --> 00:33:31,240
Sign.

353
00:33:46,400 --> 00:33:48,720
Tomorrow, I'll send someone
to handle the land transfer.

354
00:33:50,040 --> 00:33:51,760
And don't let me find out

355
00:33:51,840 --> 00:33:54,280
you're bothering Alyssa again.

356
00:34:09,320 --> 00:34:10,360
Here you go.

357
00:34:11,480 --> 00:34:13,239
-Thank you very much, Auntie.
-You're welcome.

358
00:34:15,920 --> 00:34:17,280
Kong.

359
00:34:20,199 --> 00:34:21,400
This one looks delicious too.

360
00:34:21,480 --> 00:34:22,320
Yes.

361
00:34:23,840 --> 00:34:27,520
Oh, Alyssa. Could you go buy
some noodles with gravy?

362
00:34:27,600 --> 00:34:29,920
-I'll go get some dessert for your dad.
-Okay.

363
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:31,000
Alright.

364
00:34:31,679 --> 00:34:32,960
Excuse me.

365
00:34:34,159 --> 00:34:35,880
I'd like to order--

366
00:34:40,600 --> 00:34:41,600
Thief!

367
00:34:42,719 --> 00:34:44,239
Thief!

368
00:34:50,480 --> 00:34:53,199
Alyssa! Are you okay?

369
00:34:54,080 --> 00:34:57,400
It was a snatcher.
He tried to steal my phone.

370
00:34:58,680 --> 00:34:59,840
Oh my goodness.

371
00:35:01,400 --> 00:35:04,200
-Are you hurt, Alyssa?
-I'm okay.

372
00:35:15,760 --> 00:35:17,320
Kong, hurry up!

373
00:35:17,960 --> 00:35:19,960
-Let's go!
-Whoa!

374
00:35:20,840 --> 00:35:22,960
-Hey, they're over there!
-Stop them!

375
00:35:26,400 --> 00:35:28,360
-Run!
-Don't let them get away!

376
00:35:40,400 --> 00:35:42,520
Did you get into trouble with them again?

377
00:35:43,600 --> 00:35:47,000
They started it. Look at me.

378
00:35:51,680 --> 00:35:52,840
Wee.

379
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:56,240
I'm sorry about your dad.

380
00:35:58,040 --> 00:36:00,080
Yeah, thanks.

381
00:36:01,640 --> 00:36:02,880
What are you going to do now?

382
00:36:03,960 --> 00:36:05,520
I'm thinking of dropping out.

383
00:36:06,160 --> 00:36:07,600
I'll help Mom work for now.

384
00:36:23,280 --> 00:36:25,400
Forget about that idea, Wee.

385
00:36:27,720 --> 00:36:31,520
How can you earn enough
to put both of us through school, Mom?

386
00:36:32,320 --> 00:36:35,080
We still have
the life insurance money from Dad.

387
00:36:36,280 --> 00:36:38,000
Save it for emergencies, Mom.

388
00:36:39,000 --> 00:36:40,760
I'm not good at studying anyway.

389
00:36:41,360 --> 00:36:43,760
I should work and help support the family.

390
00:36:44,560 --> 00:36:46,920
The money would be better spent

391
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:48,360
on Korn's education.

392
00:36:50,240 --> 00:36:51,800
Besides,

393
00:36:51,880 --> 00:36:55,160
I'll get a scholarship from the club.

394
00:36:55,920 --> 00:36:57,440
That'll help you too.

395
00:37:01,160 --> 00:37:03,960
I can get a part-time job
after school to help, Mom.

396
00:37:04,040 --> 00:37:05,320
No!

397
00:37:05,880 --> 00:37:08,600
You're the brains of this family.

398
00:37:08,680 --> 00:37:09,680
Just study hard.

399
00:37:09,760 --> 00:37:13,960
Once you graduate and get a good job,
you can help us then.

400
00:37:18,320 --> 00:37:19,800
Let me make this clear.

401
00:37:19,880 --> 00:37:22,840
Both of you just need to finish school.

402
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:27,280
As for the household expenses,
leave that to me.

403
00:37:29,400 --> 00:37:31,320
But where will you get the money, Mom?

404
00:37:33,320 --> 00:37:36,160
Mr. Thamrong offered me
a chance to sell food at the factory.

405
00:37:36,920 --> 00:37:40,280
If I get this job,
we'll have money coming in every day.

406
00:37:42,880 --> 00:37:45,360
Then we'll both try to save money, Mom.

407
00:37:45,960 --> 00:37:47,200
Thank you, dear.

408
00:37:51,080 --> 00:37:53,360
I have to become a first-team player.

409
00:37:53,440 --> 00:37:56,040
Then I can use my allowance
to help at home too.

410
00:37:58,640 --> 00:38:00,080
You're going to be
the national team striker?

411
00:38:00,880 --> 00:38:02,040
Yeah, I will.

412
00:38:04,680 --> 00:38:06,760
Here, eat. You talk too much.

413
00:38:13,640 --> 00:38:15,240
-Oops.
-Sorry.

414
00:38:17,600 --> 00:38:20,400
Mom, let's take a photo to remember this.

415
00:38:20,480 --> 00:38:21,360
Okay.

416
00:38:23,800 --> 00:38:26,600
-Here. Right here?
-Yes.

417
00:38:26,680 --> 00:38:27,840
Smile, Mom.

418
00:38:32,000 --> 00:38:33,200
-You look so cute.
-How is it?

419
00:38:33,840 --> 00:38:34,840
-Alright, done.
-Okay.

420
00:38:35,440 --> 00:38:38,080
-Come on. Let's go.
-Let's go.

421
00:38:43,440 --> 00:38:45,480
-Hello, Mrs. Walai.
-Hello, Mr. Thamrong.

422
00:38:45,560 --> 00:38:47,640
The manager is waiting
to taste the food now.

423
00:38:47,720 --> 00:38:48,680
Everything ready?

424
00:38:49,960 --> 00:38:51,160
We brought several dishes.

425
00:38:51,840 --> 00:38:52,720
Please come this way.

426
00:39:10,400 --> 00:39:12,520
Want to use this to hold them together?

427
00:39:12,600 --> 00:39:14,240
Thank you so much.

428
00:41:47,120 --> 00:41:49,600
The manager must have loved your cooking.

429
00:41:49,680 --> 00:41:51,360
He even asked to keep both lunch boxes.

430
00:41:51,960 --> 00:41:55,520
If they really let us sell here,
can you handle it, Mom?

431
00:41:55,600 --> 00:41:58,080
Of course I can.
Let's just hope we get the chance first.

432
00:42:05,320 --> 00:42:06,520
Hey!

433
00:42:18,400 --> 00:42:19,560
Mr. Nimit.

434
00:42:19,640 --> 00:42:23,200
Mom, call an ambulance!
Mr. Nimit has been shot!

435
00:42:25,800 --> 00:42:27,640
Mr. Nimit!

436
00:42:28,240 --> 00:42:29,800
Is he badly hurt?

437
00:42:30,840 --> 00:42:32,560
Has the ambulance arrived yet?

438
00:42:33,280 --> 00:42:35,560
Okay, I'll hurry there right now.

439
00:42:36,120 --> 00:42:38,480
Alyssa! Open the door for me, dear.

440
00:42:38,560 --> 00:42:40,640
-Alyssa!
-Yes?

441
00:42:40,720 --> 00:42:42,080
Try to stay calm, Alyssa.

442
00:42:42,160 --> 00:42:45,320
Thamrong just called and told me
your father had an accident.

443
00:42:45,400 --> 00:42:47,160
He still hasn't regained consciousness.

444
00:42:56,320 --> 00:42:57,640
Thank you.

445
00:42:57,720 --> 00:43:00,240
Uncle Thamrong said
they already caught the culprit.

446
00:43:00,320 --> 00:43:02,200
I want to see his face.

447
00:43:10,600 --> 00:43:11,880
Aunt Pat.

448
00:43:12,520 --> 00:43:15,400
This is the person
who tried to steal my phone yesterday.

449
00:43:20,040 --> 00:43:23,560
Hey! How could you be so cruel?

450
00:43:23,640 --> 00:43:26,280
What did Mr. Nimit ever do
to make you so angry

451
00:43:26,360 --> 00:43:28,560
that you'd try to kill him?

452
00:43:28,640 --> 00:43:31,760
Officer, please arrest him
and put him in jail.

453
00:43:32,360 --> 00:43:33,880
-Wait a minute, Auntie.
-Hey!

454
00:43:33,960 --> 00:43:35,880
Who are you calling auntie?
You little brat!

455
00:43:35,960 --> 00:43:39,520
You're so rude. How dare you call me that?

456
00:43:40,120 --> 00:43:42,360
Officer, lock him up
and throw away the key!

457
00:43:43,120 --> 00:43:46,200
Wait. I think there's been
a big misunderstanding.

458
00:43:47,160 --> 00:43:49,800
He's here as a witness for us.

459
00:43:53,600 --> 00:43:57,000
Here. This is the photo
that captured the culprit

460
00:43:57,080 --> 00:43:58,880
following Mr. Nimit from the factory.

461
00:43:58,960 --> 00:44:01,040
That's how we were able to catch him.

462
00:44:01,120 --> 00:44:02,480
-Oops.
-Sorry.

463
00:44:10,000 --> 00:44:14,080
-Miss, my son isn't a thief--
-Forget it, Mom.

464
00:44:14,680 --> 00:44:16,200
There's no point explaining.

465
00:44:16,280 --> 00:44:18,160
Let her think whatever she wants.

466
00:44:18,760 --> 00:44:19,800
Let's go.

467
00:44:20,480 --> 00:44:21,680
Thank you.

468
00:44:27,720 --> 00:44:31,160
The culprit is being taken
to the station now.

469
00:44:32,440 --> 00:44:35,960
Well, you should have told me sooner.

470
00:44:48,040 --> 00:44:50,600
Nuat confessed that he was hired to do it.

471
00:44:50,680 --> 00:44:52,240
But he doesn't know who hired him.

472
00:44:54,480 --> 00:44:56,800
I think it must have been Uncle Jak.

473
00:44:56,880 --> 00:44:58,600
He's upset about the land.

474
00:45:01,120 --> 00:45:03,680
The land? What land are you talking about?

475
00:45:03,760 --> 00:45:05,320
It's nothing.

476
00:45:23,480 --> 00:45:24,600
Da.

477
00:45:25,280 --> 00:45:26,800
What brings you here?

478
00:45:28,360 --> 00:45:32,440
Jak told me.
I was nearby, so I stopped by.

479
00:45:34,480 --> 00:45:35,800
How are you, Mr. Nimit?

480
00:45:36,600 --> 00:45:38,200
It's nothing serious.

481
00:45:38,280 --> 00:45:41,800
You didn't have to come visit. I feel bad.

482
00:45:41,880 --> 00:45:44,480
Don't feel bad. We're friends.

483
00:45:44,560 --> 00:45:45,920
So what did the doctor say?

484
00:45:46,000 --> 00:45:49,040
The doctor said I should stay
a night or two for observation.

485
00:45:49,120 --> 00:45:50,440
Then I'll be able to go home.

486
00:45:52,800 --> 00:45:55,160
We're getting old, Mr. Nimit.
We're not kids anymore.

487
00:45:55,960 --> 00:45:58,680
What are you talking about?
I'm still young.

488
00:45:58,760 --> 00:45:59,720
Ask my daughter.

489
00:46:01,120 --> 00:46:02,200
What?

490
00:46:03,080 --> 00:46:05,080
You've been studying in Bangkok

491
00:46:05,160 --> 00:46:08,080
and haven't even called me.
You have my number.

492
00:46:08,680 --> 00:46:12,080
I was afraid to call.
I didn't want to bother you, Aunt Da.

493
00:46:12,920 --> 00:46:17,200
How would that bother me?
You're like a daughter to me.

494
00:46:17,280 --> 00:46:19,200
If I had a son,

495
00:46:19,280 --> 00:46:21,000
I'd make him marry you.

496
00:46:29,160 --> 00:46:30,720
You're still not asleep, Mom?

497
00:46:32,480 --> 00:46:33,600
Wee, good timing.

498
00:46:34,440 --> 00:46:36,840
I wanted to tell you, after this month,

499
00:46:36,920 --> 00:46:39,560
switch Dad's phone to prepaid.

500
00:46:39,640 --> 00:46:40,720
It'll save us some money.

501
00:46:41,360 --> 00:46:43,440
Okay. I'll take care of it.

502
00:46:43,520 --> 00:46:44,720
Thanks.

503
00:46:45,480 --> 00:46:47,160
You're still not going to bed?

504
00:46:47,800 --> 00:46:51,320
I'll go once I finish this.
Just ten more minutes, dear.

505
00:46:52,640 --> 00:46:53,720
Okay.

506
00:47:04,160 --> 00:47:05,360
Mom.

507
00:47:10,440 --> 00:47:11,720
I love you.

508
00:49:07,880 --> 00:49:09,160
Korn!

509
00:49:10,880 --> 00:49:13,200
Korn!

510
00:49:14,440 --> 00:49:17,680
Mom! Something's wrong with Korn!

511
00:49:18,320 --> 00:49:20,760
Korn!

512
00:49:20,840 --> 00:49:23,160
Mom!

513
00:49:54,880 --> 00:49:56,120
Mom!

514
00:49:58,200 --> 00:50:01,040
What did the doctor say, Mom?
What's wrong with Korn?

515
00:50:04,640 --> 00:50:07,000
The doctor found a brain tumor.

516
00:50:10,920 --> 00:50:13,240
Korn's symptoms

517
00:50:13,960 --> 00:50:17,400
are caused by the tumor, which
has grown and is pressing on his brain,

518
00:50:18,240 --> 00:50:20,840
causing increased pressure
inside his skull.

519
00:50:22,320 --> 00:50:24,440
That's why he's been having
frequent headaches.

520
00:50:26,160 --> 00:50:29,080
Is there any way to cure him?

521
00:50:31,840 --> 00:50:33,000
Yes.

522
00:50:35,440 --> 00:50:39,160
But he'll need a neurosurgeon
to perform the surgery.

523
00:50:40,880 --> 00:50:43,880
Did the doctor recommend
any surgeons, Mom?

524
00:50:46,400 --> 00:50:49,240
There are a few,

525
00:50:49,320 --> 00:50:51,800
but they're at hospitals in Bangkok.

526
00:50:51,880 --> 00:50:54,000
The earliest appointment
we could get is next year.

527
00:50:55,000 --> 00:50:56,240
Otherwise,

528
00:50:57,480 --> 00:51:01,520
we'll have to get an appointment
at a private hospital.

529
00:51:03,040 --> 00:51:04,880
What if he doesn't have surgery?

530
00:51:13,200 --> 00:51:14,400
Korn's symptoms

531
00:51:15,280 --> 00:51:18,040
could become more severe.

532
00:51:18,720 --> 00:51:21,520
He might not be so lucky next time.

533
00:52:31,280 --> 00:52:33,520
What are you doing? I'm soaked!

534
00:52:33,600 --> 00:52:34,880
It's hot outside.

535
00:52:35,520 --> 00:52:36,760
It's really that hot, huh?

536
00:52:54,440 --> 00:52:57,120
What are you two even doing?
Get inside right now!

537
00:52:59,480 --> 00:53:01,320
You're a mess.

538
00:53:01,400 --> 00:53:03,280
-Careful, son.
-Hey.

539
00:53:03,360 --> 00:53:06,360
Come here. You should know better.

540
00:53:06,440 --> 00:53:08,320
You're the older brother.
Why didn't you stop him?

541
00:53:09,880 --> 00:53:11,360
Look at this mess.

542
00:53:11,440 --> 00:53:13,360
You're really making more work for me.

543
00:53:13,960 --> 00:53:15,040
Geez.

544
00:53:16,680 --> 00:53:17,840
I'm sorry, Dad.

545
00:53:19,600 --> 00:53:23,160
If Korn weren't so sickly,
Mom wouldn't be upset.

546
00:53:23,240 --> 00:53:25,400
But when he gets sick, it becomes serious.

547
00:53:27,640 --> 00:53:29,560
His health isn't very good.

548
00:53:30,520 --> 00:53:33,360
You need to help Mom and me
take special care of your brother.

549
00:53:33,440 --> 00:53:34,800
Yes, Dad.

550
00:53:46,600 --> 00:53:48,080
Feeling lonely, sick boy?

551
00:53:51,200 --> 00:53:53,000
Did you bring me any books, Wee?

552
00:53:54,080 --> 00:53:57,240
Give your brain a break.
How much are you going to read?

553
00:53:57,320 --> 00:54:00,800
You can read
when you're back home tomorrow.

554
00:54:02,720 --> 00:54:05,040
Are you staying with me tonight?

555
00:54:29,000 --> 00:54:31,000
<i>Don't tell him about this yet, Wee.</i>

556
00:54:31,880 --> 00:54:34,960
<i>Korn tends to overthink things.</i>
<i>He gets stressed easily.</i>

557
00:54:35,040 --> 00:54:38,560
<i>I don't know how much of the truth</i>
<i>he'll be able to handle.</i>

558
00:55:03,280 --> 00:55:06,400
-Somphit, could you park the car for me?
-Sure.

559
00:55:18,600 --> 00:55:19,880
Wait for me, please.

560
00:55:22,840 --> 00:55:24,120
Let me come with you.

561
00:55:38,160 --> 00:55:41,240
I'd like to leave my son with you
for a few days, Kiat.

562
00:55:41,320 --> 00:55:43,440
I have something to take care of
on Tawan Island tomorrow.

563
00:55:44,520 --> 00:55:45,800
Of course.

564
00:55:45,880 --> 00:55:47,840
Don't worry, Mr. Rawich and Mrs. Nada.

565
00:55:48,600 --> 00:55:50,280
Go take care of your business.

566
00:55:50,360 --> 00:55:52,840
We'll take good care of your son.

567
00:55:55,080 --> 00:55:58,640
He's still so young. I didn't want
to take him across to the island by boat.

568
00:55:59,320 --> 00:56:02,880
That's for the best.
The rough waves would be hard on him.

569
00:56:07,320 --> 00:56:11,280
Why don't you stay here tonight?
Leave tomorrow.

570
00:56:11,360 --> 00:56:12,440
Hey.

571
00:56:15,680 --> 00:56:19,760
He'll probably cry in a new place
without seeing his mother.

572
00:56:41,120 --> 00:56:44,680
Look at this. Look at the woman's face.
Does she look familiar?

573
00:56:46,200 --> 00:56:48,640
<i>Wee, you are my son.</i>

574
00:56:48,720 --> 00:56:52,560
<i>This house will always welcome you.</i>

575
00:56:52,640 --> 00:56:54,920
<i>I have a brain tumor, right?</i>

576
00:56:55,000 --> 00:56:56,560
<i>The doctors are looking for a treatment.</i>

577
00:56:56,640 --> 00:56:59,240
Don't be afraid, Korn.
You're going to get better.

578
00:57:00,480 --> 00:57:03,920
How much do you two want for your trouble?

579
00:57:04,000 --> 00:57:06,680
I'll pay you, and we can end this.
No need to get involved any further.

580
00:57:08,320 --> 00:57:10,240
-Let go!
-Stay still!

581
00:57:10,320 --> 00:57:11,920
Run!

582
00:57:13,640 --> 00:57:17,240
Mrs. Walai, could you tell me
the whole story again?

583
00:57:24,000 --> 00:57:25,720
Take Alyssa back to Bangkok tomorrow.

584
00:57:25,800 --> 00:57:27,400
I'll handle her withdrawal.

585
00:57:27,480 --> 00:57:30,160
<i>I'm sending her to study in America.</i>

586
00:58:09,440 --> 00:58:11,160
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
